{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue moved from $41.9 billion in FY2016 to $47.9 billion in FY2025, a 1.5% CAGR [F1][F10][F219]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was a step down then a rebuild: revenue fell 13.5% in FY2017 and 5.3% in FY2018 before recovering to $45.8 billion by FY2023 [D42][D93][F8]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2017 decline came with refranchising of bottling operations, which cut operating cash flow that year [P75]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income compounded at 5.3% against revenue's 1.5%, and net income at 8.1%, so profit outgrew the top line over the window [F221][F219][F222]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2025 was the sharpest inflection, with operating income up 37.7% on lower other operating charges after the prior-year fairlife contingent consideration remeasurement [D450][P12]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Concentrate operations supplied 59.4% of FY2025 revenue and 1.6pp of its 1.9% growth, while finished product operations added 0.3pp [D532][D534][D449][D541]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Within concentrate, the non-US piece contributed 1.3pp of FY2025 growth on 3.1% growth, and US concentrate added 0.3pp [D548][D547][D569]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Non-US finished product operations shrank 4.9% and subtracted 1.0pp, offsetting part of the concentrate gain [D554][D555]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Worldwide concentrate sales volume grew 1% in FY2025, with EMEA up 4% and pricing favorable, per the filing [P12][P10]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 37.7% against 1.9% revenue growth, an incremental margin of 428.4%, so operating leverage was extreme but driven by the charge comparison [D450][D449][D473]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
